.TH SPLICE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
splice \- Linux x86-64 syscall 275
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_260_299.h>
.B ssize_t splice(int input, off_t* input_offset, int output, off_t* output_offset, size_t length, unsigned int flags);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Transfers bytes between descriptors, at least one of which must be a pipe.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR splice (2)
